% Table of the numbers 1-9 divided by 10. Chace vol. II pl. 33, PDF pp. 113-114 ("Table of division by 10", beside 2 ÷ 101); Peet p. 50 (Pl. F, New York fragment 6).
% Read from page images by a coding agent's sub-agent; no person checked it. See sources/notes/table-2n-b.md.
% The papyrus gives only the values, all in black, with no dividends: two columns, 1-6 down the first, 7-9 down the
% second, so that its rows 1-3 each carry two entries (1 and 7, 2 and 8, 3 and 9). The headings n ÷ 10 are ours.
% Chace: "The surviving portions of this example and table ... are all from the New York fragments."

1 ÷ 10
'10

2 ÷ 10
'5

3 ÷ 10
'5 '10

4 ÷ 10
'3 '15

5 ÷ 10
'2

6 ÷ 10
'2 '10

7 ÷ 10
2/3 '30           % Chace n. 4: "The '30 in line 1 is correctly reproduced on Peet's Plate E but appears as restored on his Plate F, and in his text, page 50."; Peet p. 50: 2/3 ['30]

8 ÷ 10
2/3 '10 '30

9 ÷ 10
2/3 '5 30         % Chace n. 4: "The same fraction in line 3 appears correctly on Peet's Plate F, where he has restored the fractional dot omitted by the scribe, and in his text, but his Plate E shows '10."; Peet p. 50: 2/3 '5 '30
